<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.relay.fm/focused/261">On this episode of <em>Focused</em></a>, Mike and I take apart our complicated relationship with measurement. We start with Goodhart&#8217;s Law, the idea that a number stops measuring the thing you cared about the moment it becomes the target, and follow that through law school rankings and grades.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Metrics can be useful, but are also dangerous. In this episode we explain why.</p>



